A||||3||new fiero||Front wiring harness||||5||
Z||000000||new fiero||07-13-2001||12:09 AM||||This should be an easy one for this group.<P>I want to upgrade by installing power windows in my 86.  Do I need to get a whole new front harness from a donor car or are there multiple harnesses for accessories like power windows and locks??<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jim Jimenez||07-13-2001||01:25 AM||||I just did this in my '88 formula as well as adding factory air and cruise. The power window harness stretches from the console up behind the dash, and runs in the same channel as the courtesy light/door jamb switch wiring. It is separate from the main harness. You will also need the junction block that snaps into the side panel above the fuse box in you have no other power accessories<P>Good luck--Happy Fieroing<P>------------------<BR>Jim J||||reg||6
Z||000002||DRH||07-13-2001||01:56 AM||||I just added PW, PDL and PM to my Formula also. Just like Jim said. The PM harness is by itself. The PDL and PW harness are together and only include a couple of extra wires for the door switches and courtesy lights. Your car will have a small harness with just these few wires. Get all the wiring for the power stuff from the donor. There's a harness in each door and a harness that runs all the way across the dash and to the center console. You shouldn't have to cut any wires, it's all plug and play. Mine already had the junction box. It's a white plastic box way up above the fuse box.<P>I would recommend taking the dash out rather than trying to get to everything from below.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||new fiero||07-13-2001||08:39 AM||||Thanks guys.....Great info!<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||1
